-- title:
--   Every homogeneous piece of $R[\tau,V]/(\tau^2V-v)$ lies in $\tau^iV^hR$ for one monomial $\tau^iV^h$
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $v \in R$, and let $T_v = R[X_0,X_1]/(X_0^2X_1 - v)$. Write $\tau$ and $V$ for the classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, so that $\tau^2 V = v$ in $T_v$, and identify every $s \in R$ with its image in $T_v$. Give $T_v$ the $\mathbb{Z}$-grading in which $R$ has degree $0$, $\tau$ has degree $-1$ and $V$ has degree $2$: for $e \in \mathbb{Z}$, the homogeneous piece $(T_v)_e$ is the image in $T_v$ of the polynomials that are weighted homogeneous of weight $e$ for the weights $\mathrm{wt}(X_0) = -1$, $\mathrm{wt}(X_1) = 2$. Equivalently, $(T_v)_e$ is the $R$-linear span of the monomials $\tau^a V^b$ with $2b - a = e$. Since the relation $X_0^2X_1 - v$ has weight $0$, this is a grading of $T_v$.
--
--   For every integer $e$ there are natural numbers $i$ and $h$, depending only on $e$, such that every homogeneous element of degree $e$ is an $R$-multiple of the monomial $\tau^i V^h$:
--
--   $$
--   \forall\, e \in \mathbb{Z}\ \ \exists\, i, h \in \mathbb{N}\ \ \forall\, r \in (T_v)_e\ \ \exists\, s \in R:\qquad r = \tau^i V^h s .
--   $$
--
--   In other words, each homogeneous piece of $T_v$ is contained in the cyclic $R$-submodule $\tau^i V^h R$ generated by a single monomial. This uniform statement is the form in which the grading is used when extracting derivations: if a derivation $D$ of $T_v$ sends all of $R$ into one fixed piece $(T_v)_j$, then all values $D(s)$, $s \in R$, share the common factor $\tau^i V^h$, and the restriction of $D$ to $R$ can be divided by it.
--
--   **Formalization Note** No hypothesis is placed on $R$ beyond commutativity, and none on $v$. The piece $(T_v)_e$ is `pieces R v e`, the image of `weightedHomogeneousSubmodule R weight e` (with `weight = ![-1, 2]`) under the quotient map `π R v`, and the scalar $s$ enters through `algebraMap R (T R v)`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Algebra/AffineCancellation/ModificationGrading.lean#L113-L125

